        "text": "Since the RSI is a momentum indicator, it shows the rate, or the momentum at which the price is changing. This means that if momentum is increasing while the price is rising, the uptrend is strong and more and more buyers are stepping in. In contrast, if momentum is decreasing while the price is rising, it may show that sellers might soon take control over the market. A traditional interpretation of the RSI is that when it's over 70, the asset is overbought, and when it's under 30, it is oversold. As such, extreme values may indicate an impending trend reversal or pullback. The second indicator is called the moving average. A moving average smooths out price action by filtering out market noise and highlighting the direction of the trend.",
        "start": 480,
        "end": 41650,
        "confidence": 0.98189104,
        "channel": null,
